# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH, 6-31G, GNOF, FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE with CHOLESKY TRUE,
# including C4_SPINOR -- the Cholesky-vector counterpart of lih_gnof_c4_full_optimization.inp.
#
# C4_DHF's MO integrals span an enormous dynamic range (the negative-energy branch's diagonal is
# order -2mc^2, ~1e4 Hartree, next to the chemically-scaled positive-energy block): decomposing
# the two blocks together directly would let the negative branch's sheer magnitude dominate the
# pivoted decomposition's pivot selection and starve the (chemically relevant) positive-energy
# block's own reconstruction accuracy (confirmed directly: ~3.5e-05 instead of the ~1e-15 CHOLESKY
# already achieves for NON_REL/X2C). Since occupations are EXACTLY 0 on the negative branch, no
# energy/gradient/Hessian sum ever needs its TRUE integral values anyway -- runFullOptimizationJk/
# Pnof therefore zero that block out before decomposition (not merely excluding it from the
# accuracy check), eliminating the mixed-scale competition entirely and recovering the same
# ~1e-12-1e-15 reconstruction accuracy as the other two paths, at roughly half as many vectors as
# decomposing the untouched full tensor would need. Compare the converged energy against
# lih_gnof_c4_full_optimization.inp's own dense-integral result (they agree to ~1e-9 Hartree).
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
C4_SPINOR TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
CHOLESKY TRUE

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
